; Desktop Subsystem for Android (DSA)
; What the kernel's own threads do that the platform's policy does not expect.

; The guest kernel keeps devtmpfs, and its kdevtmpfs thread adds a node to it for each device
; the kernel finds after the policy is loaded. Android never mounts that devtmpfs: init mounts
; a tmpfs on /dev and ueventd makes the nodes there. The platform's policy does not let the
; kernel write devtmpfs's root, so each node was refused, and the denials (over a hundred a
; boot) filled the kernel's audit queue before logd read it. The nodes are not needed, so the
; refusal stays and is not logged.
(dontaudit kernel device (dir (write add_name create search)))
(dontaudit kernel device (chr_file (create setattr getattr)))
(dontaudit kernel device (blk_file (create setattr getattr)))
